Routing this as research, round: the question is whether to replace our search engine, it's costly to get wrong, and nothing is decided yet. I can't read or write files in this session, so I can't write the round brief here. Once the repository is reachable, I'll write it to `docs/rounds/`, and it will test the options against our search quality and cost before anyone commits.

My early view, before the round: a vector database is usually an addition to keyword search, not a replacement. Hybrid retrieval often beats either alone on document search with citations, so I'd expect the round to test that first. Routing accuracy is NOT ESTABLISHED, so correct me in one line if this is the wrong size.

